fact WorkItem(id: "WI-586", description: some(value: "Codegen (Rust): guard per-op method type-params against name collision with the enclosing trait's type params. emit_trait_method (anthill-core/src/codegen/rust.rs) emits per-op generics verbatim (e.g. <Acc>); a spec 'operation foo[T](...)' inside 'sort Stream[T, E]' would emit 'fn foo<T>(...) -> Box<dyn Stream<T, E>>' where the method T shadows the trait T and mis-binds the return. No current trigger — found by WI-553 code-review. Mirror the delivered WI-579 C++ fix which seeded the member-template canonicaliser against the class params. Rust-only."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
